%SIXMD 1
# @?LOGIN - AUTHENTICATE A USER ON A TERMINAL

## @?OPTIONS

## @?OPERANDS

### @?TTY
NUMERIC TERMINAL IDENTIFIER.  INIT SUPPLIES THIS OPERAND WHEN IT STARTS LOGIN.

## DESCRIPTION

LOGIN CREATES A TERMINAL SESSION, PROMPTS FOR AN ACCOUNT NAME AND PASSWORD,
SETS THE ACCOUNT UID AND GID, CHANGES TO THE ACCOUNT HOME DIRECTORY, AND
REPLACES ITSELF WITH THE CONFIGURED LOGIN SHELL.

LOGIN IS NORMALLY STARTED BY INIT RATHER THAN BY AN INTERACTIVE USER.

## @?FILES

### @?/CONFIG/PASSWD
ACCOUNT DATABASE USED FOR AUTHENTICATION, HOME DIRECTORY, AND LOGIN SHELL.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?1 - SESSION ENDED OR FAILED
LOGIN EXITS WHEN TERMINAL SETUP, AUTHENTICATION SESSION SETUP, OR SHELL EXEC
FAILS.  INIT NORMALLY RESPAWNS IT.
